From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:12:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 002/138] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-n61: Add DRV2604 haptics

The iPhone 6 has a TI DRV2604 haptic driver at address 0x5a on i2c1,
with its enable line on GPIO 76, driving a linear resonant actuator.
Both are taken from the Apple device tree (i2c1/vib-pwm).

LRA mode was confirmed on hardware: auto-calibration passes (STATUS
0x80) and the motor vibrates, whereas ERM mode fails calibration.

The rated and overdrive voltages match what Apple's iOS 12.5.5 driver
(AppleDRV2604Vibrator) programs: RATED_VOLTAGE = 0x61 and OD_CLAMP =
0x97. With drv260x's mV * 255 / 5600 conversion, 2140 mV and 3320 mV
yield exactly those register values.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts
index 10b4ca8ba..5eec5926c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts
@@ -7,8 +7,24 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include "t7000-6.dtsi"
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/ti-drv260x.h>
 
 / {
 	compatible = "apple,n61", "apple,t7000", "apple,arm-platform";
 	model = "Apple iPhone 6";
 };
+
+&i2c1 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	haptics@5a {
+		compatible = "ti,drv2604";
+		reg = <0x5a>;
+		enable-gpios = <&pinctrl 76 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		mode = <DRV260X_LRA_MODE>;
+		library-sel = <DRV260X_LIB_LRA>;
+		vib-rated-mv = <2140>;
+		vib-overdrive-mv = <3320>;
+	};
+};
